# CODEOWNERS - who must approve changes to which files (GitLab syntax).
#
# In a real repository this file lives at the repository root, in docs/ or in
# .gitlab/ (the first one found wins). Here it sits inside the project as
# documentation of the pattern, with paths written as if this project were the
# repository root. Requires GitLab Premium or Ultimate.
#
# Settings that must be ON for this file to be enforced
# (Settings → Repository → Protected branches; Settings → Merge requests):
#   - main: "Allowed to push and merge" = No one   (unset is NOT restricted -
#           anyone who may push directly skips every approval rule)
#   - main: "Require approval from code owners"
#   - "Prevent editing approval rules in merge requests"
#   - "Prevent approvals by users who add commits"
#   - restrict who may unprotect the branch
#
# Matching rules:
#   - A leading "/" anchors the pattern at the root. Without it, the pattern
#     matches at any depth ("all.yml" would match every all.yml anywhere).
#   - A trailing "/" covers the directory and everything below it.
#   - Inside one section, the LAST matching entry wins.
#   - Separate [sections] are enforced independently: a file matched in two
#     sections needs an approval from each. Keep overrides in the same section.

[Ownership]
# Default: the platform team owns everything, including this file.
/CODEOWNERS                               @platform-team
/site.yml                                 @platform-team
/ansible.cfg                              @platform-team
/collections/                             @platform-team
/roles/                                   @platform-team
/inventory/                               @platform-team

# Component-test override. Same section, later line, so the component team is
# the only required owner of its own group_vars file. Everything else - all.yml,
# hosts.yml (group membership = which hosts are affected), roles/ - stays with
# the platform team. The line is added in the merge request that creates the
# test group and removed in the one that promotes it (README: "Testing a new
# component version").
/inventory/group_vars/sshd_hardening_test.yml  @sshd-team
